  "plan": {
    "goal": "Perfuse a liver-on-chip to reproduce reported hepatic sinusoidal wall shear stress of 0.05 Pa.",
    "rationale": "Hepatic sinusoidal wall shear is very low (~0.05-0.15 Pa per the physiology registry for HepG2). We target the lower end, 0.05 Pa. In a 400 µm wide x 100 µm high x 20 mm PDMS channel with water-like medium (viscosity 1e-3 Pa·s), the flow rate that yields 0.05 Pa wall shear is 2.0 µL/min (computed via flow_rate_for_shear_stress and confirmed by wall_shear_stress = 0.05 Pa). Reynolds number is 0.13 (laminar), residence time ~24 s, pressure drop ~20 Pa (well within syringe-pump range). HepG2 seeded at 75,000 cells/cm² (midpoint of the 5e4-1e5 registry range) on the 0.08 cm² channel floor = 6000 cells. O2 supply/demand ratio ~14 at the upper OCR bound (4.7 nmol/min/1e6 cells), so the perfused design is not hypoxic.",
